  "worked_solution": "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $\u27e8\\cdot ,\\cdot \u27e9$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\u2016f(t)\u2016=\\sqrt{\u27e8f(t),f(t)\u27e9}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8f(t),f(t)\u27e9 & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\,{(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\,({cos}^{2}\u2061t+{sin}^{2}\u2061t-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(1-\\operatorname{sin}\u20612t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u20612t}{2}){|}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\pi +\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u20612\\pi }{2})-((-\\pi )+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-2\\pi )}{2}) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we made use of the trigonometric identities\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}\u2061t+{cos}^{2}\u2061t=1\\,\\text{and}\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u20612t=2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nFinally then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016f(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{2\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
